    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "У нас проблема с заказом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We have a problem with our order.' the guest uses the classic Russian possession phrasing — literally 'at us' rather than a verb meaning 'to have', pairing it with 'problem' and 'order'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Я просил без лука.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I asked for no onions.' the guest chooses the imperfective verb meaning 'ask for' for the ongoing action, followed by 'onion'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Уважаемые.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Excuse me.' the guest delivers a punchy conversational reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'respected'.",
      "gap": 0.4
